Package: runix
Type: Package
Title: Common Core for the Runix System-Administration Framework
Version: 0.0.1.12
Date: 2026-08-17
Authors@R: c(
    person("Troy", "Hernandez", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "troy@cornball.ai",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-4248-604X")),
    person("cornball.ai", role = "cph"))
Description: The near-zero-dependency common core shared by the Runix subsystem
    packages: the typed condition taxonomy and constructor, a retryability
    registry, the subsystem-neutral injectable-runner machinery (environment
    and error class supplied by the caller), the neutral result object, a
    deterministic JSON-line encoder, the durable-audit sink (append-only
    JSONL with two-phase intent/outcome correlation, advisory locking, fsync,
    rotation, and honest persistence reporting), and the AF_UNIX client for the
    privileged audit broker. Subsystem packages ('pkgstate', 'rsystemd', ...)
    import this; it never imports them, and its only dependency is 'janssonr'
    for strict parsing and validation of broker responses (the Jansson library
    the broker daemon itself uses). This is a Unix package (it
    administers a Linux host); the broker client is Linux-only, returning a
    typed 'runix_broker_unavailable' on other Unix platforms where
    system-durable audit is reported absent, while the core, memory sink, and
    portable file-sink guarantees remain available.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
OS_type: unix
Imports: janssonr (>= 0.0.1.1)
Additional_repositories: https://cornball-ai.github.io/drat
SystemRequirements: coreutils 'sync' (for fsync/fdatasync of the audit sink
    and its parent directory); Linux procfs '/proc' for audit lock-owner
    liveness, boot id, and process start time (absent elsewhere, lock
    staleness degrades to an mtime timeout); the audit broker client uses
    AF_UNIX and is Linux-only (absent elsewhere); libjansson (>= 2.11,
    'libjansson-dev' on Debian/Ubuntu) linked into the C core for strict,
    in-C parsing of broker responses on the effect-receipt path, so the
    single-use effect receipt and outcome binding are extracted and wiped in
    C and never become R objects.
Suggests: tinytest
Encoding: UTF-8
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
